<title>SOUTH AFRICA: INTRUST BUYS STAKE IN SAFLIFE.</title>
<headline>INTRUST BUYS STAKE IN SAFLIFE.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's Investec Investment Trust Ltd (Intrust) said on Thursday that it had agreed to buy five million shares in Saflife Ltd for 80 million rand from Investec Bank Ltd .</p>
<p>Saflife is the holding company for AGA Holdings Ltd, which is a financial services group.</p>
<p>Intrust said the historical performance of Saflife was not seen as a good indicator of its future prospects and the group is confident the buy will make a positive contribution to Intrust's earnings.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
